# =============================================================================
# What is excluded, and why.
#
# Two categories only: things GitHub will not accept, and things that are
# rebuildable from what IS committed. Nothing analytical is excluded — every
# script, query, config, output and document that constitutes the work is
# tracked.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Exceeds GitHub's limits --------------------------------------------
# The DuckDB warehouse is ~154MB. GitHub hard-blocks single files over 100MB
# and warns above 50MB. It is fully rebuildable:
#   python3 scripts/build_warehouse.py
nhs_warehouse.db
*.db
*.db.wal
*.db.wal.stale*

# ---- Rebuildable source data (~135MB) -----------------------------------
# Raw NHS England downloads. Reproducible from the URL manifests that ARE
# committed (scripts/rtt_urls.txt, dm01_urls.txt, ae_urls.txt, gpad_urls.txt)
# plus scripts/download_rtt.sh. Committing 135MB of third-party open data that
# anyone can re-download would bloat the clone for no benefit.
data_raw/

# ---- Build and editor noise ---------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/

# ---- Scratch and render artefacts ---------------------------------------
docs/_preview/
docs/_p2/
docs/_c2/
docs/_chk/
*.tmp

# ---- Excel and Tableau lock files ---------------------------------------
~$*.xlsx
~$*.docx
*.twbr
